Description:
  Adds a Content Security Policy violation report endpoint and shows the
  reports on the backstage Security page. Needs maquina:security, whose
  `security` database stores them.

  Installs CspReportsController (POST <path>, no session or CSRF, both report
  formats, 64 KB cap, browser-extension noise dropped), the
  Security::CspViolation model and its migration in db/security_migrate, the
  csp_violations table in db/security_schema.rb, a daily purge in
  config/recurring.yml and a section on the Security page. It points the
  policy's report-uri at the endpoint, gives anonymous requests a nonce
  (Rails' session-id nonce is empty without a session), exempts the endpoint
  from the general Rack::Attack throttle and caps it on its own. Anything it
  cannot place safely is listed after the install instead of being forced.

Examples:
  rails g maquina:csp_reports
  rails g maquina:csp_reports --path /security/csp-reports
